.\" improv-files(5): the files Improv reads and writes.
.TH IMPROV-FILES 5 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv-files \- Improv's model file, CSV import format and DuckDB model text
.SH DESCRIPTION
Improv keeps a model in a store: a Mentat file or a Postgres database. It
reads tables from CSV and TSV files, and the DuckDB extension reads a model
from a short text.
.SH THE MODEL FILE
A store file is an SQLite database holding a Mentat datom store: each fact
is an entity, attribute and value. Every front end
.RB ( improv (1),
.BR improv-tui (1),
.BR improv-gui (1),
.BR improv-server (1))
opens it by path; opening one creates it and installs the schema. An empty
path is an in-memory store. The attributes:
.TP
.BR :category/id ", " :category/name
A category (a dimension).
.TP
.BR :item/id ", " :item/name ", " :item/category
An item, a member of one category.
.TP
.BR :measure/id ", " :measure/name ", " :measure/value-type ", " :measure/categories ", " :measure/category-order ", " :measure/kind ", " :measure/formula
A measure:
.B input
or
.BR derived ,
its categories and their order, and a derived measure's formula as JSON.
.BR :measure/description " and " :measure/sql-source
are optional.
.TP
.BR :cell/key ", " :cell/measure ", " :cell/coord ", " :cell/value-number ", " :cell/value-boolean ", " :cell/value-text
One input cell: its measure, its coordinate (JSON) and its value.
.TP
.BR :view/id ", " :view/json
A saved view.
.TP
.BR :meta/external-fns ", " :meta/external-calls ", " :meta/scenarios ", " :meta/lambdas
The model's external functions,
.B CALL(...)
measures, scenarios and named LAMBDAs, as JSON.
.PP
A save writes only the cells that changed. A save fails, writing nothing,
when another writer has saved since this one loaded the model: reload and
edit again.
.B MENTAT_MMAP_SIZE
sets how many bytes of the file SQLite memory-maps
.RB ( 0 :
none).
.PP
A model kept in Postgres is named by a URL,
.BI postgres:// user @ host / db ?model= name\fR,
and lives in the
.B improv
schema's catalog tables (the same catalog
.BR pg_improv (7)
uses).
.SH CSV AND TSV IMPORT
.B improv import-csv
reads one table into a new input measure:
.IP \(bu 2
The first row names the columns, unless
.B \-\-no\-header
is given; then columns are 0-based indices.
.IP \(bu 2
Fields are separated by commas, or by tabs with
.B \-\-tsv
or when the file name ends in
.BR .tsv .
Quoting is RFC 4180's: a field in double quotes may hold the separator, a
newline, or
.B \(dq\(dq
for a quote.
.IP \(bu 2
Each dimension column
.RI ( col : cat-id : cat-name )
supplies a category; its distinct values become items, reusing an item that
already has the name. The value column must be a number in every row.
.IP \(bu 2
A short row, a non-numeric value, more than 10,000,000 records, a field over
1 MiB or a record over 64 MiB is an error, and nothing is imported.
.PP
.B improv export-csv
writes the same layout: one column per category, then the value, header row
first. Text a spreadsheet would run as a formula
.RB ( = ,
.BR + ,
.BR \- ,
.B @
first, or a tab or carriage return) is written with a leading quote.
.SH DUCKDB MODEL TEXT
The DuckDB extension's
.BI improv( source ", " model )
table function reads a model as text, one item per line:
.PP
.RS
.nf
category Time = year
category Product = product
input Price = price max
input Quantity = qty sum
Revenue = Price * Quantity
.fi
.RE
.TP
.BI category " Name " = " column"
A category made from a column: its distinct non-NULL values, in the
column's order.
.TP
.BI input " Name " = " column " "\fR[\fBsum\fR|\fBavg\fR|\fBmin\fR|\fBmax\fR|\fBcount\fR]"
An input measure over every category. Two source rows on one coordinate are
an error unless an aggregation is named.
.TP
.IB Name " = " formula
A derived measure, as in
.BR improv-formulas (7).
.PP
Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
or
.B \-\-
are ignored; keywords are case-insensitive; a column name with spaces or
capitals goes in double quotes. The result has a row per derived cell:
.BR measure ,
one column per category,
.B value
and
.BR value_text .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR improv (1),
.BR improv-import-csv (1),
.BR improv-export-csv (1),
.BR improv-formulas (7),
.BR pg_improv (7).
